        About Michael
      </h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-start mb-12">
        <div class="space-y-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-parchment/60">
          <p>My work with young men began long before formal counselling registration.</p>
          <p>As a teenager, I entered a deep process of mentorship, psychological work, and personal development myself under the guidance of forensic psychologist Bernard Altman through the organisation Boys to Men. Over the years, that gradually evolved into leadership, facilitation, mentorship, and direct work with large numbers of adolescent and young adult men navigating identity, emotional struggle, belonging, conflict, responsibility, direction, masculinity, and the difficult transition into adulthood.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl text-parchment/80 leading-snug">
            Much of what shapes a young man's life happens in the spaces where he feels he cannot speak honestly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Background panels -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-12">
        <div class="border border-parchment/10 rounded-xl p-6 bg-header/20">
          <p class="font-heading text-xs text-primary/60 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Experience With Young Men</p>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-parchment/50 leading-relaxed">
            For years, I worked closely within Boys to Men in group facilitation, mentorship, developmental process work, emotional reflection, and youth leadership under Bernard Altman's guidance. This work exposed me to a wide range of young male struggles: withdrawal, anger, confusion, identity conflict, self-esteem difficulties, family tension, lack of direction, emotional shutdown, and the quiet loneliness many young men carry beneath the surface. Communities I worked in included Ocean View, Lavender Hill, and Hanover Park.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-parchment/10 rounded-xl p-6 bg-header/20">
          <p class="font-heading text-xs text-primary/60 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Counselling and Developmental Approach</p>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-parchment/50 leading-relaxed">
            I am registered with the ASCHP as a Wellness Counsellor. My approach integrates reflective counselling, developmental mentorship, nervous system awareness, embodied practice, emotional reflection, behavioural observation, and practical life-oriented guidance. The emphasis is not on fixing people or imposing ideology, but on helping individuals gradually develop greater awareness, responsibility, emotional maturity, groundedness, and psychological stability within their own lives.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-parchment/10 rounded-xl p-6 bg-header/20">
          <p class="font-heading text-xs text-primary/60 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Meditation and Embodied Practice</p>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-parchment/50 leading-relaxed">
            Over recent years, I have also spent extensive time in India studying and practising meditation, breathwork, yoga, contemplative psychology, and embodied awareness practices under experienced teachers and within traditional settings. These elements are not approached as dogma or spiritual performance. Where relevant, they are integrated carefully and practically as tools for attention, nervous system regulation, emotional awareness, self-observation, grounding, and inner stability.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Philosophical and ethical panels -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-10">
        <div class="border border-parchment/10 rounded-xl p-7 bg-header/15">
          <p class="font-heading text-sm text-parchment/75 mb-4">A Grounded Approach To Mentorship</p>
          <div class="space-y-3 font-body text-xs text-parchment/50 leading-relaxed">
            <p>I do not believe young men need endless shaming, performance pressure, emotional suppression, or rigid identity systems in order to mature. Nor do I believe all struggle should immediately be pathologised.</p>
            <p>In many cases, young men need something both simpler and more demanding: honest relationship, clear reflection, accountability, guidance, challenge, self-awareness, and meaningful opportunities to consciously participate in shaping who they are becoming.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-parchment/10 rounded-xl p-7 bg-header/15">
          <p class="font-heading text-sm text-parchment/75 mb-4">Scope and Responsibility</p>
          <div class="space-y-3 font-body text-xs text-parchment/50 leading-relaxed">
            <p>This mentorship work is developmental and relational in nature. It is not a substitute for psychiatric care, emergency psychological intervention, addiction treatment, or specialist clinical services where these are required.</p>
            <p>Where appropriate, referrals or collaborative support with other professionals may be recommended.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4 font-body text-sm text-parchment/55 leading-relaxed mb-8">
        <p>At its core, this work is about helping young men gradually become more honest with themselves, more emotionally grounded, more capable of responsibility, and more able to consciously shape the direction of their lives.</p>
        <p>Not through force. Not through performance. But through relationship, reflection, challenge, practice, and trust built carefully over time.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl text-parchment/75 leading-snug max-w-xl mb-10">
        A young man does not become mature merely because time passes. Maturity must be consciously developed, embodied, and lived.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-8">
        <span class="px-4 py-1.5 border border-parchment/15 rounded-full text-xs font-body text-parchment/40 tracking-wide">ASCHP Registered Reg.&nbsp;10559</span>
        <span class="px-4 py-1.5 border border-parchment/15 rounded-full text-xs font-body text-parchment/40 tracking-wide">Yoga Alliance RYS&nbsp;300</span>
        <span class="px-4 py-1.5 border border-parchment/15 rounded-full text-xs font-body text-parchment/40 tracking-wide">Online worldwide</span>
        <span class="px-4 py-1.5 border border-parchment/15 rounded-full text-xs font-body text-parchment/40 tracking-wide">Currently accepting new clients</span>
